Stuart Wheaton wrote:
> Usually when I find a poly trap, I get changed into a newt or such like 
> and die practically before I can step off the thing...But last night, my 
> Valkyrie suddenly found herself turned into a silver Dragon. 

Nice. Check out the #monster and #sit commands.

> This is 
> cool.  Now I might even live to do what has always been impossible, 
> actually ascending.

Probably not. A high-level valk does more damage, has more HP, a better 
AC and is faster than any dragon. Being a dragon is fun nonetheless.

>  What do I need to worry about when I'm a Dragon?

You have a bite attack, so stay away from 'trices and green slimes. 
Also, you don't have hands, so opening doors and manupulating objects 
can be tricky; besides your god will consider not having hands a minor 
trouble and might turn you back into a human if you pray. Also, dragons 
fly, so don't worry about trapdoors (you can still dive in by pressing 
">"), but do worry about sinks (bead pun, but it might hurt) and, if a 
female dragon, you can lay (hatchable) egs by #sit-ing. Oh, and before I 
forget, dragons are quite slow, so don't try to run away or chase 
something; use your breath attack instead.

> Does this wear off, or can I toss my old armor and stuff?

It does wear off. Unfortunately, the more powerful the monster, the 
faster the polymorph wears off. As Zeitgeist said, an amulet of 
unchanging might help.

